{
  "id": "focus",
  "order": 16,
  "title": "Szórend: a fókusz",
  "titleEn": "Word order: the focus position",
  "level": "A1",
  "lesson": "l08-szorend",
  "summary": "The most important word goes directly in front of the verb. Everything else is fairly free.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Hungarian word order isn't about subject–verb–object. It's about **what matters most**. That word goes in the **focus position: right before the verb**."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Three things always sit in focus: **new information**, a **question word**, and the negative word **nem**."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "head": [
        "",
        "Focus",
        "Verb",
        "Rest"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Question",
          "**Hol**",
          "él",
          "Petra?"
        ],
        [
          "Answer",
          "**Varsóban**",
          "él.",
          "(Petra)"
        ],
        [
          "Question",
          "**Ki**",
          "tud",
          "törökül?"
        ],
        [
          "Answer",
          "**Hakan**",
          "tud",
          "törökül."
        ],
        [
          "Negative",
          "**Nem**",
          "beszélek",
          "oroszul."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Same words, different meaning"
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "hu": "Péter kávét iszik.",
          "en": "Peter drinks COFFEE (not tea).",
          "note": "kávét is in focus"
        },
        {
          "hu": "Péter otthon dolgozik.",
          "en": "Peter works AT HOME (not somewhere else).",
          "note": "otthon is in focus"
        },
        {
          "hu": "Petra japánul beszél.",
          "en": "Petra speaks JAPANESE (and not Chinese)."
        },
        {
          "hu": "Petra jól beszél japánul.",
          "en": "Petra speaks Japanese WELL."
        },
        {
          "hu": "Petra beszél jól japánul.",
          "en": "PETRA speaks Japanese well (not Éva)."
        },
        {
          "hu": "Én vagyok Kis Kornél.",
          "en": "I am Kornél Kis. (It's ME you're looking for.)"
        },
        {
          "hu": "Kis Kornél vagyok.",
          "en": "I'm Kornél Kis. (normal introduction)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "text": "Yes/no questions use statement order: *Petra jól beszél japánul?* Only the melody rises."
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "tone": "warn",
      "text": "In a neutral statement, the part that answers the (unspoken) question is the focus: — Milyen nyelven beszéltek otthon? — **Németül** beszélünk otthon. Saying *Beszélünk németül otthon* sounds odd."
    }
  ]
}